  "details": "- CVE-2026-73072: fix heap buffer overflow in set_sofo(); reset sl_sal_first[] before the SN_SOFO\n  counting loop, since a preceding SN_SAL section may have set its entries to -1 via set_sal_first(),\n  making the loop under-count colliding multi-byte characters and allocate an undersized list\n  (src/spellfile.c, upstream patch 9.2.0846)\n- CVE-2026-73076: fix arbitrary code execution via a crafted .VimballRecord file; refuse to extract\n  a member named .VimballRecord, record deletions with string() instead of raw quote interpolation,\n  and execute only whitelisted call delete() entries in vimball#RmVimball()\n  (runtime/autoload/vimball.vim, upstream patch 9.2.0847)\n- CVE-2026-73078: fix Ex command injection in the netrw bookmark and history menus; add the Ex\n  separator | to g:netrw_menu_escape, escape the :e targets with fnameescape(), and quote the\n  netrw#MakeTgt() arguments with string() (runtime/autoload/netrw.vim, upstream patch 9.2.0840)",
